@kind(api)

@meta{
  crate: tomet-compute
}

=[ tomet-compute ]

==[ tomet-compute ]

Expression evaluation for `${...}` interpolation expressions ([`InterpExpr`])
and built-in math functions.

==[ Architecture & Responsibilities ]

- Pure Compute Boundary (Zero I/O):

`tomet-compute` performs dynamic expression evaluation for Tomet interpolation
expressions (`${...}`). It performs zero I/O: identifier and member lookups
(`${node.member}`) are delegated to `tomet-address::resolve_reference`.

- Expression Evaluation:
  - [ `Literal`: Evaluates directly to [`Value::Int`], [`Value::Float`], or [`Value::String`].
      `Identifier` / `Member`: Resolves against [`Document`] through `tomet_address`.
      `Call`: Recursively evaluates argument expressions, then dispatches to builtin functions. ]

- Builtin Numeric Functions:

`add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div`, `mod`. Type promotion produces integers when both arguments
are integers, or floats when mixing. Integer overflow automatically promotes to `f64`
rather than panicking. `div` provides true division (e.g. `div(7, 2)` produces `3.5`).

==[ Structs ]

===[ struct EvaluationContext ]

An evaluation context carrying dynamic variables and parameters (e.g. for template instantiation).

==[ Functions ]

===[ fn evaluate ]

Evaluates `expr` against `doc`. `Literal`s evaluate to themselves;
`Identifier`/`Member` chains resolve via
`tomet_address::resolve_reference` (falling back to `@config` macros for bare identifiers);
a `Call` dispatches to builtins or `@config` user-defined macros after evaluating its args.

===[ fn evaluate_with_config ]

Evaluates `expr` against `doc` using an explicitly supplied [`tomet_semantics::DocumentConfig`].

===[ fn evaluate_with_vars ]

Evaluates `expr` against `doc` using an explicit variables map.

===[ fn evaluate_with_context ]

Evaluates `expr` against `doc` using a [`tomet_semantics::DocumentConfig`] and an [`EvaluationContext`].
